<title>SWEDEN: SSAB blames steel prices for lower 9-mo.</title>
<headline>SSAB blames steel prices for lower 9-mo.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish steelmaker SSAB on Thursday posted a sharp fall in earnings for the first nine months of the year, blaming lower prices and volumes for the fall but saying the steel market had now stabilised.</p>
<p>The company repeated its forecast of halved profits for 1996 compared with 1995 levels of 3.83 billion crowns ($584.4 million). ($ = 6.553 Swedish Crowns)</p>
</text>
